ad. También revisar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en distintas áreas. Verificar si los contratos de diciembre se relacionan con otros adjudicatarios.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 89 minor contracts for works above 37,500 and up to 40,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 13.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 6.5, with a 95% confidence interval of 4.7 to 9.0. December accounts for 2% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 16% of all its works contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 26. Contract [1], for 39,343.29 euros, was awarded in May 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the legal limit does not prove improper actions. It could reflect market pricing, budget constraints, or multiple separate needs. Statistical patterns alone do not indicate wrongdoing without further evidence.\nWhat can be checked: Check the details of contract [1] to confirm the work scope and dates. Verify if awardee A has other contracts for similar services. Ensure that multiple contracts for the same need were not awarded in a short period.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"obras","citas":["1RYBnyXYRoRLAIVZdUs8KA%3D%3D","mzCD7AzMoaS7JOCXkOhcDg%3D%3D","JH1exxOfy%2BeopEMYCmrbmw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}